<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>

	<!--
		Dead Man's Switch: automatroid modification items (heavy hydraulic frame, ceramic plates, synthetic tendon, armor
		plating, subsonic module and the rest of BaseModificationItem's children) no longer turn up at tribal traders.
		This folder only loads when Dead Man's Switch is active (see loadFolders.xml).
		  - Their shared parent BaseModificationItem tags them Serum. Vanilla's neolithic base trader and shaman caravan stock
		    the Serum tag with no tech cap (it is how tribals sell serums), so every tribe sold them. The tag becomes
		    ExoticMisc, which the outlander base, outlander exotic caravan, orbital and Empire traders also stock, so the
		    high-tech outlets stay. Modded Serum-only traders (Det's Keshig, Forsaken, Leo - Events' black market) stop
		    carrying them; Cinders of the Embergarden's outlander base stocks ExoticMisc too, so it keeps them.
		  - The parent gets techLevel Industrial when it has none, so tech-capped stock generators can tell what they are.
		    Children that set their own tech level keep it.
		Dead Man's Switch's own code never reads the Serum tag; its supply-chain quest picks these items by category.
		The nuclear battery carries Serum on its own def but is Sellable (traders buy it, never stock it), so it is left alone.
		Verified 2026-10-28 against Dead Man's Switch 1.7: BaseModificationItem (in Defs/Things_Item/DMS_Modification.xml) has
		tradeTags Serum, tradeability Buyable and no techLevel; its 9 children set no tradeTags or techLevel of their own.
		The 1.6 release has no BaseModificationItem, so in the 1.6 copy both operations find nothing and do nothing.
	-->
	<Operation Class="PatchOperationSequence">
		<operations>
			<li Class="PatchOperationConditional">
				<xpath>Defs/ThingDef[@Name="BaseModificationItem"][tradeTags/li[text()="ExoticMisc"]]/tradeTags/li[text()="Serum"]</xpath>
				<match Class="PatchOperationRemove">
					<xpath>Defs/ThingDef[@Name="BaseModificationItem"][tradeTags/li[text()="ExoticMisc"]]/tradeTags/li[text()="Serum"]</xpath>
				</match>
			</li>
			<li Class="PatchOperationConditional">
				<xpath>Defs/ThingDef[@Name="BaseModificationItem"]/tradeTags/li[text()="Serum"]</xpath>
				<match Class="PatchOperationReplace">
					<xpath>Defs/ThingDef[@Name="BaseModificationItem"]/tradeTags/li[text()="Serum"]</xpath>
					<value>
						<li>ExoticMisc</li>
					</value>
				</match>
			</li>
			<li Class="PatchOperationConditional">
				<xpath>Defs/ThingDef[@Name="BaseModificationItem"][not(techLevel)]</xpath>
				<match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
					<xpath>Defs/ThingDef[@Name="BaseModificationItem"][not(techLevel)]</xpath>
					<value>
						<techLevel>Industrial</techLevel>
					</value>
				</match>
			</li>
		</operations>
	</Operation>

</Patch>
